  ⚠ oxc(prefer-array-to-reversed): Use `arr.toReversed()` instead of copying and reversing.
   ╭─[prefer_array_to_reversed.tsx:1:18]
 1 │ const reversed = arr.slice().reverse();
   ·                  ─────────────────────
   ╰────
  help: Copying and then calling `reverse()` allocates an extra array. `toReversed()` returns a reversed copy in one step.

